tests/ir/fusion_entrywise.sky:8:5: note: [FUSE-001] `sqrt(x * x + y * y) * k + d` is rewritten to `fused(x, y, k, d)`
  |
8 | r = sqrt(x * x + y * y) * k + d
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: applied by the `fuse` pass
  = note: because fused 6 elementwise operations into one kernel; saves 5 temporary arrays of 3 elements
  = note: because every intermediate result is used exactly once, by the next operation, and every array operand is a Vector[3]
  = note: because 6 of the operations can fail (`mul`, `add`, `math.sqrt`); the kernel reports the failure of the first of them in program order that fails at any element, which is the error the separate operations gave

tests/ir/fusion_entrywise.sky:8:5: note: [PAR-003] this elementwise kernel over 3 elements is not parallelized: it may fail and is small
  |
8 | r = sqrt(x * x + y * y) * k + d
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: because 3 elements is under the threshold of 683: splitting it across threads costs more than it saves

tests/ir/fusion_entrywise.sky:9:5: note: [FUSE-001] `atan2(y, x) / %23` is rewritten to `fused(y, x, %23)`
  |
9 | q = atan2(y, x) / [2, 2, 2]
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: applied by the `fuse` pass
  = note: because fused 2 elementwise operations into one kernel; saves 1 temporary array of 3 elements
  = note: because every intermediate result is used exactly once, by the next operation, and every array operand is a Vector[3]
  = note: because 2 of the operations can fail (`math.atan2`, `div`); the kernel reports the failure of the first of them in program order that fails at any element, which is the error the separate operations gave

tests/ir/fusion_entrywise.sky:9:5: note: [PAR-003] this elementwise kernel over 3 elements is not parallelized: it may fail and is small
  |
9 | q = atan2(y, x) / [2, 2, 2]
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: because 3 elements is under the threshold of 2048: splitting it across threads costs more than it saves

