   = note: because every intermediate result is used exactly once, by the next operation, and every array operand is a Vector[3]
   = note: because 3 of the operations can fail (`mul`, `div`, `add`); the kernel reports the failure of the first of them in program order that fails at any element, which is the error the separate operations gave

